{
  "description": "VTC1 raw-TCP data-plane frame encodings, byte-exact. Both the Android and Windows implementations must encode each 'input' to exactly 'frameHex', and decode 'frameHex' back to 'input'. See ProjectInfo/04-PROTOCOL.md section 7.3.",
  "wireFormat": "magic 'VTC1' (4) | type u8 (1) | transferIdLen u16 BE (2) | transferId UTF-8 (N) | seq u64 BE (8) | payloadLen u32 BE (4) | payload (M). All integers big-endian. String lengths inside payloads are u16 BE, except Chunk.dataLen which is i32 BE.",
  "derivation": "Expected bytes were assembled field-by-field from the section 7.3 table by an independent PowerShell byte-stream script that links against neither implementation. They were then cross-checked against the C# codec. Two independent constructions agreeing is the point; a vector captured from one implementation would only encode that implementation's bugs.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "TransferEnd, completed",
      "input": { "type": "TransferEnd", "seq": 1, "transferId": "tx1", "completed": true },
      "expected": { "frameHex": "5654433107000374783100000000000000010000000101", "frameLength": 23 },
      "layout": [
        "56544331          magic 'VTC1'",
        "07                type = TransferEnd",
        "0003              transferIdLen = 3",
        "747831            'tx1'",
        "0000000000000001  seq = 1",
        "00000001          payloadLen = 1",
        "01                completed = true"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Chunk, two data bytes",
      "note": "payloadLen = 12 + dataLen = 14 (0x0e). Chunk is the only frame whose inner length field is i32 rather than u16.",
      "input": { "type": "Chunk", "seq": 2, "transferId": "t", "itemIndex": 0, "chunkIndex": 1, "dataHex": "aabb" },
      "expected": { "frameHex": "565443310400017400000000000000020000000e000000000000000100000002aabb", "frameLength": 34 },
      "layout": [
        "56544331          magic",
        "04                type = Chunk",
        "0001              transferIdLen = 1",
        "74                't'",
        "0000000000000002  seq = 2",
        "0000000e          payloadLen = 14",
        "00000000          itemIndex = 0",
        "00000001          chunkIndex = 1",
        "00000002          dataLen = 2",
        "aabb              data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ItemBegin",
      "note": "Payload is fixed at 20 bytes (0x14). It carries no relative path and no hash; those travel on the control plane.",
      "input": { "type": "ItemBegin", "seq": 7, "transferId": "ab", "itemIndex": 3, "sizeBytes": 1024, "chunkCount": 2, "chunkSize": 512 },
      "expected": { "frameHex": "5654433103000261620000000000000007000000140000000300000000000004000000000200000200", "frameLength": 41 },
      "layout": [
        "56544331          magic",
        "03                type = ItemBegin",
        "0002              transferIdLen = 2",
        "6162              'ab'",
        "0000000000000007  seq = 7",
        "00000014          payloadLen = 20",
        "00000003          itemIndex = 3",
        "0000000000000400  sizeBytes = 1024",
        "00000002          chunkCount = 2",
        "00000200          chunkSize = 512"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth over LAN_TCP",
      "note": "Route byte: 0x01 = WIFI_DIRECT, 0x02 = LAN_TCP. payloadLen = 2+3+2+3+1 = 11 (0x0b).",
      "input": { "type": "Auth", "seq": 1, "transferId": "x", "authToken": "tok", "senderDeviceId": "dev", "route": "LAN_TCP" },
      "expected": { "frameHex": "565443310100017800000000000000010000000b0003746f6b000364657602", "frameLength": 31 },
      "layout": [
        "56544331          magic",
        "01                type = Auth",
        "0001              transferIdLen = 1",
        "78                'x'",
        "0000000000000001  seq = 1",
        "0000000b          payloadLen = 11",
        "0003              tokenLen = 3",
        "746f6b            'tok'",
        "0003              devIdLen = 3",
        "646576            'dev'",
        "02                route = LAN_TCP"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "AuthAck, ok, no reason",
      "note": "An absent reason is encoded as a zero length, not omitted. payloadLen = 1+2+0 = 3.",
      "input": { "type": "AuthAck", "seq": 2, "transferId": "x", "ok": true, "reason": null },
      "expected": { "frameHex": "5654433102000178000000000000000200000003010000", "frameLength": 23 },
      "layout": [
        "56544331          magic",
        "02                type = AuthAck",
        "0001              transferIdLen = 1",
        "78                'x'",
        "0000000000000002  seq = 2",
        "00000003          payloadLen = 3",
        "01                ok = true",
        "0000              reasonLen = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ItemEnd",
      "note": "The hash travels as a UTF-8 hex STRING with a u16 length, not as 32 raw bytes. A real frame carries 64 characters; this vector uses 'ab' to keep the derivation checkable by eye.",
      "input": { "type": "ItemEnd", "seq": 3, "transferId": "x", "itemIndex": 0, "sha256Hex": "ab" },
      "expected": { "frameHex": "56544331050001780000000000000003000000080000000000026162", "frameLength": 28 },
      "layout": [
        "56544331          magic",
        "05                type = ItemEnd",
        "0001              transferIdLen = 1",
        "78                'x'",
        "0000000000000003  seq = 3",
        "00000008          payloadLen = 8",
        "00000000          itemIndex = 0",
        "0002              hashLen = 2",
        "6162              'ab'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ItemResult, failed with error",
      "input": { "type": "ItemResult", "seq": 4, "transferId": "x", "itemIndex": 1, "ok": false, "error": "E" },
      "expected": { "frameHex": "56544331060001780000000000000004000000080000000100000145", "frameLength": 28 },
      "layout": [
        "56544331          magic",
        "06                type = ItemResult",
        "0001              transferIdLen = 1",
        "78                'x'",
        "0000000000000004  seq = 4",
        "00000008          payloadLen = 8",
        "00000001          itemIndex = 1",
        "00                ok = false",
        "0001              errLen = 1",
        "45                'E'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Cancel",
      "input": { "type": "Cancel", "seq": 5, "transferId": "x", "reason": "no" },
      "expected": { "frameHex": "565443310800017800000000000000050000000400026e6f", "frameLength": 24 },
      "layout": [
        "56544331          magic",
        "08                type = Cancel",
        "0001              transferIdLen = 1",
        "78                'x'",
        "0000000000000005  seq = 5",
        "00000004          payloadLen = 4",
        "0002              reasonLen = 2",
        "6e6f              'no'"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "boundsVectors": [
    { "name": "empty transferId is rejected", "input": { "transferId": "" }, "expected": { "reject": true, "reason": "transferIdLen must be 1..256" } },
    { "name": "transferId of 257 bytes is rejected", "input": { "transferIdLength": 257 }, "expected": { "reject": true, "reason": "transferIdLen must be 1..256" } },
    { "name": "bad magic is rejected", "input": { "firstByteOverwrittenWith": "00" }, "expected": { "reject": true, "reason": "expected 'VTC1'" } },
    { "name": "clean EOF at a frame boundary yields no frame, not an error", "input": { "stream": "empty" }, "expected": { "frame": null } },
    { "name": "stream closing mid-frame is an error", "input": { "stream": "frame truncated by one byte" }, "expected": { "reject": true, "reason": "stream closed prematurely" } }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Chunk frames must NOT auto-flush; every other frame type must. The caller owns the flush cadence for bulk data.",
    "payloadLen is bounded at 16 MiB and transferIdLen at 256 bytes. Both are enforced on read before any allocation.",
    "seq is monotonic per sender and is carried on every frame, including Chunk. A frame format without it cannot detect a reordered or truncated stream.",
    "The first C# implementation of this codec omitted transferId and seq from the header entirely, used u32 where the wire uses u16, and gave Chunk a byte offset instead of a chunk index. It passed all of its own round-trip tests. That is the reason this file exists."
  ]
}
